@startuml components
!include style.iuml
left to right direction
title LazyFinance — Components / Logical View

component "<b>Angular web — apps/ui</b>\nPublic prerender / private CSR\nFinance pages and persistent assistant" as Web <<boundary>>
component "<b>External MCP client</b>\nOwned reads / delegated changes" as Client <<external client>>

package "Public API — apps/api" <<application>> {
  component "<b>API adapters</b>\nPublic tRPC / text and voice streams\nSeparate OAuth + MCP boundary" as Gateway <<boundary>>
  component "<b>Shared financial services</b>\nBalances, movements, tags and income\nBudgets, measured savings and evidence\nBounded preview / action policy" as Core <<domain core>>
  component "<b>Assistant workflow</b>\nGrounded text / optional live voice control\nOwned history and proposal preparation" as Assistant <<first-party agent>>
  component "<b>Identity and consent</b>\nVerified subject → internal owner\nClient-bound grants and scopes" as Auth <<security>>
  component "<b>Banking orchestration</b>\nLifecycle, explicit selection and aliases\nShared prepared snapshot synchronization" as Banking <<adapter>>
  component "<b>Banking scheduler</b>\nOpt-in Fintoc only\nDurable due claim, no browser required" as Schedule <<adapter>>
}

component "<b>Private persistence — apps/persistence</b>\nAssertion / purpose / owner validation\nFactual projections and named commands\nHistory, grants and atomic action receipts" as Stored <<persistence>>
database "<b>PostgreSQL 18</b>\nidentity / finance / assistant\nExact facts, constraints and forced RLS" as DB

component "<b>Firebase Auth</b>\nFirst-party identity verification" as Firebase <<security>>
component "<b>Configured model provider</b>\nText model / OpenAI Realtime\nDisabled by default" as Model <<model provider>>
component "<b>Fintoc</b>\nProvider-neutral banking adapter" as Fintoc <<adapter>>

Web ..> Gateway : public tRPC / NDJSON
Client ..> Gateway : MCP OAuth
Gateway --> Core
Gateway --> Assistant
Gateway --> Auth
Gateway --> Banking
Schedule --> Banking : selected enrollment
Schedule ..> Stored : narrow claim purpose
Assistant --> Core : read / propose / status
Core ..> Stored : signed private tRPC
Assistant ..> Stored
Auth ..> Stored
Banking ..> Stored
Stored --> DB : scoped SQL
Assistant ..> Model
Auth ..> Firebase
Banking ..> Fintoc

legend bottom
  One shared API financial core serves web, assistant and MCP; only private persistence owns SQL.
  Private RPC signs user context or a narrow purpose: identity, OAuth, banking claim or transport admission.
  Assistant proposals need UI approval; MCP writes require separate scopes. The model has no execution authority.
  The development-only simulated bank uses owned source records and the same ingest/commit path, without automatic sync.
  No money movement. Model / provider calls never hold a SQL transaction open.
endlegend
@enduml
